🚀 Step 3: Wrap Password Input
Instead of having only the input,

<input ... />
we'll wrap it inside a container.

<div className="password-input">
    <input
        type={showPassword ? "text" : "password"}
        placeholder="Password"
        value={password}
        onChange={(e) => {
            setPassword(e.target.value);
            setPasswordError("");
            setFormError("");
        }}
    />

    <button
        type="button"
        className="eye-btn"
        onClick={() => setShowPassword(!showPassword)}
    >
        {showPassword ? <FaEyeSlash /> : <FaEye />}
    </button>
</div>
🧠 Why did we add a <div>?
Think of it like this.

Earlier:

Password

+-----------------------+
| ***************       |
+-----------------------+
Now we need

+------------------------------+
| ***************         👁    |
+------------------------------+
The input and eye icon need to stay inside one box.

That box is:

<div className="password-input">
🚀 Step 4: CSS
Add this to signup.css.

.password-input{
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
}
Now the input.

.password-input input{
    width:100%;
    padding:13px 45px 13px 14px;
}
Notice

padding-right:45px;
Why?

Because the eye icon needs space.

Otherwise

Password123👁
would overlap.

Now the eye button.

.eye-btn{
    position:absolute;
    right:14px;
    top:50%;
    transform:translateY(-50%);
    background:none;
    border:none;
    cursor:pointer;
    color:#6b7280;
    font-size:18px;
}
🎓 Let's Understand position
This is one of the most important CSS concepts.

Imagine your password box is a room.

+------------------------------+
|                              |
|                              |
|                              |
+------------------------------+
When we write

.password-input{
    position:relative;
}
we are telling CSS:

"This room is the reference point."

Now

.eye-btn{
    position:absolute;
}
means:

"Place this object somewhere inside that room."

Then

right:14px;
means

14px

|

↓

+-----------------------------+
|                      👁      |
+-----------------------------+
And

top:50%;
transform:translateY(-50%);
centers it vertically.

