JWT Authentication

Login

↓

Token

↓

Store Token

↓

Protected Dashboard
This is how real companies build authentication systems.

📌 My suggestion
Since you've completed the Login page, I recommend we don't spend more time adding mock login conditions. They won't exist in the final application anyway.

Instead, let's move on to building the Dashboard UI (Create Capsule, My Capsules, Profile, Logout). Once the backend is ready, we'll connect the Login page to a real Spring Boot API and replace the mock logic with actual authentication.

That way, you're building features that will stay in the final project rather than temporary code.


