🧠 New React Concept
Until now you've built pages using repeated HTML.

Now we'll learn Reusable Components.

Instead of writing this four times:

<div className="card">
we'll create one reusable component:

<DashboardCard />
and use it like this:

<DashboardCard
    title="Create Capsule"
/>

<DashboardCard
    title="My Capsules"
/>

<DashboardCard
    title="Profile"
/>

<DashboardCard
    title="Logout"
/>
This is how professional React developers build applications.

Why is this better?
Without reusable components:

Card
Card
Card
Card
Lots of duplicate code.

With reusable components:

DashboardCard

↓

Reuse × 4
One component.

Four uses.

Cleaner.

🎯 Our Next Lesson
In the next step, we'll build our first reusable React component called:

DashboardCard.jsx
You'll learn:

✅ Props (one of the most important React concepts)

✅ Component Reusability

✅ Passing data from parent to child

✅ Click events on cards

✅ Navigation from cards

