🧠 New React Concept
You have already learned:

State

↓

Props

↓

Routing
Today you're learning something very important.

Passing Functions as Props
Earlier we passed

title="Profile"
Now we're passing

onClick={() => navigate("/profile")}
Notice this is a function, not text.

Inside DashboardCard

<div

className="dashboard-card"

onClick={onClick}

>
React says

"When someone clicks me,

execute whatever function my parent gave me."

This is called

Callback Props
You'll see this in every React project.

